<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef sharply higher on light demand and very light offerings.  Select and Choice rib, round and loin cuts higher, while chuck cuts sharply higher. Beef trimmings higher on mostly moderate demand and light offerings. - USDA</p>
<p>---</p>
<p>215 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p> 23 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>40 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     105.94	105.33	100.95	100.64</p>
<p>Changes	   2.45	  2.49	  2.41	  2.18</p>
<p>Rib	  157.80	157.41	145.32	145.21</p>
<p>Chuck	 74.74	 71.42	 75.58	 73.19</p>
<p>Round	 91.63	 91.63	 90.90	 90.90</p>
<p>Loin	 168.05	170.03	150.72	152.74</p>
<p>Brisket     62.79	 62.79	 62.66	 62.66</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  70.56	 70.47	 70.85	 70.65</p>
<p>Flank	 58.65	 58.65	 57.59	 57.59</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
